                                "sense_id": "8baabd75-5847-3aea-9ad5-e40fc61a5040",
                                "text": "1589, Richard Hakluyt, The Principal Navigations, Voyages, Traffiques and Discoveries of the English Nation\n... and there is a fulle fair vale and a fructuouse, and there is a fair cytee and a gode, that men clepen Neople."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4d1a37e1-e24c-461a-a7d4-2c0cea1ee785",
                                "sense_id": "8baabd75-5847-3aea-9ad5-e40fc61a5040",
                                "text": "As fruits of hotter countries, transearthed in colder climates, have vigour enough in themselves to be fructuous according to their nature: but, that they are hindered by the chilling nips of the air, and the soil, wherein they are planted."
                            }
